# Student Roster Display Names

When showing a **student** name anywhere in the app (cards, chips, tables, dialogs, print, toasts, confirmations), use `getRosterDisplayName` from `@/lib/roster/roster`.

It prefers roster `firstName`/`lastName` (with the class name format), then falls back to account `name` / email / the unnamed label.

```ts
import {
  getRosterDisplayName,
  type RosterNameFormat,
} from "@/lib/roster/roster";

const displayName = getRosterDisplayName(
  student,
  t("unnamedMember"),
  nameFormat, // from the class when available
);
```

## Do

- Pass the class `RosterNameFormat` when you have it (`resolveRosterNameFormat` / class settings).
- Use a translated unnamed fallback (e.g. `t("unnamedMember")`).
- Reuse this helper in print/export paths too (`groupsPrint`, etc.).

## Don't

```ts
// ❌ BAD — skips roster first/last and class name format
student.name
getDisplayName(student, t("unnamedMember"))
`${student.firstName} ${student.lastName}`
```

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
getRosterDisplayName(student, t("unnamedMember"), nameFormat)
```

`getDisplayName` from `@/lib/user/userDisplay` is for non-roster users (teachers, generic members). Do not use it as the primary path for students who may have roster name fields.
